fix-tpm-st-unmarshal: accept every TPM_ST value when unmarshaling a TPM_ST

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

Spec (TPM 2.0 Part 2, TPM_ST, "Table: Definition of (UINT16) TPM_ST
Constants"): the table lists the TPM_ST values and has no "#TPM_RC_VALUE"
row, i.e. unmarshaling a TPM_ST performs no value check. The structures that
need a particular tag check it themselves, e.g. Part 2, TPMT_TK_VERIFIED,
"Table: Definition of TPMT_TK_VERIFIED Structure":
  "tag | TPM_ST | ticket structure tag"
  "#TPM_RC_TAG | | error returned when *tag* is not one of the values in
   @tbl:tpm-st-for-signatures"
and Part 2, TPMT_TK_CREATION, "Table: Definition of TPMT_TK_CREATION
Structure":
  "tag {TPM_ST_CREATION} | TPM_ST | ticket structure tag"
  "#TPM_RC_TAG | | error returned when *tag* is not TPM_ST_CREATION"

TPM_ST (Part 2, "TPM_ST Constants") has no #TPM_RC_VALUE, so unmarshaling a
TPM_ST accepts any value, as the TCG reference does; structures that require
a specific tag check it themselves (the tickets, TPMT_TK_*, return
TPM_RC_TAG). Upstream returned TPM_RC_VALUE for values that are not TPM_ST
constants, so e.g. TPM2_PolicyAuthorize or TPM2_CertifyCreation with a ticket
tag such as 0x0303 failed with TPM_RC_VALUE instead of TPM_RC_TAG (found by
differential fuzzing). Command tags are unaffected
(bug-fix-command-tag-unmarshal.patch); TPMI_ST_ATTEST is output-only.

